§§ `Article 12(3) — the advance on compensation for health and life`

-- Within 3 working days of receiving the buyer's or insured's notice of the accident (the
-- deadline is in nd67-art12-duties-workdays.l4), the insurer must advance:
-- (a) where the accident has been found within the scope of compensation: 70% of the estimated
--     compensation for one person for a death; 50% for a partial injury ("tổn thương bộ phận");
-- (b) where it has not yet been: 30% of the limit per person for a death or an estimated injury
--     rate of 81% or more; 10% of the limit for an estimated rate from 31% to under 81%.
-- Fork F15: point (b) joins "tử vong và ước tính tỷ lệ tổn thương từ 81% trở lên" with "và"; read
-- as two cases (a death; an estimate of 81% or more), not as both at once.
-- Fork F16: a persistent vegetative state is Part A item 2 of Annex VI and ALSO Part B section I
-- item 4.1, so it is a partial injury for point (a), and an estimated rate of 100% for point (b).
-- An estimated rate under 31% where the scope has not been found is none of the cases (b) lists:
-- the clause then requires no advance.
